new file mode 100644
index 0000000..df2fe44
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/perf_bench/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# perf_bench
+
+Benchmark app for the JS-thread measurement spike. Findings:
+`experiments/interop/reports/10-js-thread.md` (in the main checkout).
+
+It is a real solid-fuse app (bundle built by `fuse build`, QuickJS engine,
+Flutter Linux desktop) with a Dart driver that runs scenarios, takes timings on
+both sides of the bridge and prints one `BENCH {json}` line per measurement.
+
+## Layout
+
+| Path | What |
+|---|---|
+| `src/harness.ts` | JS-side timing (`performance.now()` inside QuickJS), op and byte counting around `fjs.bridge_call` |
+| `src/screens.tsx` | Part 1: card screens, one-signal updates, keyed lists, JSON payloads |
+| `src/box.tsx` | Part 2: the curated `Box` component five ways (hand-written `View`, mapped in Dart, three TS wrappers, composed from generated primitives) |
+| `src/interact.tsx` | Parts 3 and 5: drag, scroll-linked header, upper-casing text field, each JS-driven and Dart-owned |
+| `src/index.tsx` | Command table driven from Dart over the `bench` channel |
+| `src/_generated/`, `dart/lib/_generated/` | `fuse gen` output for the 12 primitives in `fuse.config.ts` |
+| `dart/lib/bench_widgets.dart` | Bench-only native widgets: `benchBox` (the curated layer in Dart), probes, Dart-owned interactions |
+| `dart/lib/harness.dart` | Dart-side timing: op receipt, apply, frame start/end, `FrameTiming`, UI-isolate heartbeat, synthetic pointer input |
+| `dart/lib/suite_basic.dart` | Parts 1, 2, 4 |
+| `dart/lib/suite_interact.dart` | Parts 3, 5 |
+| `tools/run.sh`, `tools/run-all.sh` | Run suites under xvfb, save `BENCH` lines |
+| `tools/aggregate.py` | `BENCH` lines to the markdown tables in the report |
+| `tools/run-in-bun.ts` | Load the bundle in Bun with a stub bridge (debugging; not QuickJS numbers) |
+| `results/` | Raw output of the runs the report quotes |
+
+Framework changes this needs (all in `packages/solid-fuse`, same branch):
+`FuseRuntime.perfOnOps` / `perfChannels` (instrumentation hook) and a fix for
+keyed list moves (`applyOps` disposed a node on `remove` even when the same
+batch re-inserted it; see the report).
+
+## Rerun
+
+```bash
+export PATH=/opt/flutter/bin:$PATH
+bun install                                   # repo root
+(cd packages/solid-fuse && bun run build)     # solid-fuse dist
+
+cd examples/perf_bench
+bun fuse link                                 # once: pub get, pubspec_overrides
+bun fuse gen                                  # only if fuse.config.ts changed (about 35 s)
+bun fuse build --js-only                      # production bundle -> dart/assets/js/bundle.js
+(cd dart && flutter build linux --release --no-tree-shake-icons)   # first build compiles the Rust engine
+
+tools/run.sh part1 7 results/part1-x.txt      # one suite: part1..part5, or `smoke`
+NICE=-10 tools/run-all.sh x                   # everything, about 35 minutes
+python3 tools/aggregate.py results/*-x.txt    # tables
+```
+
+`--profile` works the same way (`flutter build linux --profile ...`, then
+`tools/run.sh part1 7 out.txt profile`). In profile and debug builds
+`host.mode` is not `release`, so the renderer also tracks the owning component
+of every node; release is the mode the report quotes.
+
+`REPS` is the second argument. Each suite prints raw records; nothing is
+averaged in the app.
+
+## What a record contains
+
+For an operation followed to the frame (`measure` in `harness.dart`):
+
+| Field | Meaning | Clock |
+|---|---|---|
+| `jsMs` | uninterrupted JS: the operation, Solid's flush, and handing the op batch to the bridge | `performance.now()` in QuickJS |
+| `sendMs` | the part of `jsMs` spent inside `fjs.bridge_call` (JS value to Rust value) | same |
+| `ops`, `bytes`, `kinds` | ops in the batch; `bytes` is `JSON.stringify(ops).length`, from a separate pass with `detail` on | |
+| `callMs` | Dart `await channels.call(...)` for the command | `Timeline.now` |
+| `toRecvMs` | command sent to Dart's `_ops` handler entered | `Timeline.now` |
+| `decodeMs` | how long the UI isolate's event-loop turn had already run when `applyOps` started: receiving and decoding the batch. Resolution about 1 ms | 1 ms heartbeat |
+| `applyMs` | `FuseRuntime.applyOps` | `Timeline.now` |
+| `uiFrameMs` | begin-frame to post-frame callback of the frame that shows the ops: build, layout, paint | `Timeline.now` |
+| `e2eMs` | command sent to that frame finished on the UI thread | `Timeline.now` |
+| `uiMaxStallMs` | longest gap of the 1 ms heartbeat during the operation | |
+| `ft` | `FrameTiming` figures for the frames in the window (raster is llvmpipe software rendering: not representative) | engine |
+| `load` | 1-minute load average when the record was taken | `/proc/loadavg` |
+
+Interaction records (`drag`, `scroll`, `text_*`) are described at the top of
+each `run*` function in `suite_interact.dart`.
